# Build output
*.exe
*.dll
*.o
*.a
build/

# The submission archive and any staging folder for it. The finished zip is
# 82 MB, most of it the Stockfish binary, and GitHub rejects pushes over 100 MB
# anyway - it is built from the whitelist in docs/PLAN.md when needed.
*.zip

# The Stockfish engine binary only - 98 MB, past GitHub's per-file limit. It is
# shipped in the submission zip and recoverable anyway: the README records its
# version and SHA-256.
#
# The path is written out in full, and anchored with a leading slash, because
# the bare pattern "stockfish*" that used to be here also matched
# client/StockfishEngine.cpp and client/StockfishEngine.h - git on Windows has
# core.ignorecase=true, so it ignores case when matching. Those two files were
# silently missing from every commit until it was noticed. Stockfish's licence
# and AUTHORS files stay tracked: they are tiny, and the GPL requires them to be
# shipped with the binary.
/stockfish/stockfish.exe

# Tool and editor local state - never part of the project
.claude/
.vs/
*.bak
*~

# One-off environment setup leftovers
setup_chess.bat
setup_log.txt
setup_done.marker

# NOTE: .vscode/ and CLAUDE.md ARE tracked, on purpose. Git is the off-machine
# backup, and anything ignored here is not backed up. Both are excluded from
# the submission zip manually instead - see docs/PLAN.md Phase 7.
